he county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair came in at 42% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026 it has swung the other way, with May to June at 205% of normal and April to May at 156%. All 6 grids had their driest year in 1954.</p>"}
